          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ferveō is an inherited verb (EtymDB). English fervent comes from it, and ferment from its noun fermentum."
            }
          ]
        },
