              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ēlixus, ēlixa, ēlixum — \"boiled\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Carō ēlixa mollis et dulcis erat. The boiled meat was soft and sweet."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Boiled right through. A slave in Plautus jokes that he tastes better boiled than roasted."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ēlixus is built, says Lewis & Short, on ē, \"out, thoroughly\", and lix, an old word for water or lye: thoroughly boiled."
            }
          ]
        },
